{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545419-who-are-the-strangers-from-vda20-companion-s-followers-of-set-apocrypha","id":1545419,"title":"Who are the Strangers from VDA20 Companion's Followers of Set Apocrypha?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-05T17:54:16-08:00","id":1545419,"title":"Who are the Strangers from VDA20 Companion's Followers of Set Apocrypha?","content":"Hello there!<br /> <br /> The question is as in the thread's title. The Strangers are introduced on p.130:<br /> <br /> \u201cHe saw beings in the dark beyond, mighty as gods but fragile as gossamer before the finished portions of the world. These strangers, these kings beyond the desert wished to introduce their own true names, which would contradict the names of the created world. They searched for flaws in the Nine\u2019s names, in Creation, so that they might introduce their own words, their Chaos-names.&quot;<br /> <br /> To me, they sound a bit like the Children that Baali worship or try to keep asleep (depending on the faction), the Earthbound, but there are (as always) discrepancies: the FoS Apocrypha distinguishes between demons and the Strangers; Baali lore suggests the Earthbound have been in the Earth from possibly longer than Set and Caine; the Strangers seem separate from Creation, trying to get a foothold in it through the Names, but the Earthbound, while asleep, seem pretty entrenched in Creation. <br /> <br /> The Nine, including Set, are described as sorcerers in the story, so I think it's a fair assumption that they are Ascended Mages or something like that.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 11-05-2024, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T16:04:53-08:00","id":1545538,"title":"","content":"It sounds like it could be a setting-appropriate version of the Aeons, the spiritual enemies of the clan in a number of earlier Setite clanbooks. The Aeons' nature is ambiguous enough that their true nature could be completely up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T21:09:14-08:00","id":1545550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545419-who-are-the-strangers-from-vda20-companion-s-followers-of-set-apocrypha?p=1545538#post1545538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like it could be a setting-appropriate version of the Aeons, the spiritual enemies of the clan in a number of earlier Setite clanbooks. The Aeons' nature is ambiguous enough that their true nature could be completely up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like the best solution, at least at the table. Depending on the ST or chronicle the nature of the Aeons can shift to what the game involves itself with and what makes the best story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T22:55:42-08:00","id":1545556,"title":"","content":"I think the Aeons are more about order and control, and are connected to Osiris, Ra, and the rest of the Egyptian pantheon, therefore they would be more like a later way of framing the Nine. As for the Strangers, they seem much more chaotic in nature.<br /> <br /> A box in that section offers suggestions on how to use this story in one's games, and one idea that is mentioned is that they may be connected to the same entities with whom the Baali are involved, as I said also in the OP. I may need to reread the Baali lore given in VDA20: perhaps they have been redefined slightly in a way that would make sense with this association.<br /> <br /> Part of the game lore, even in VDA20, is that Setites are particularly averse to the Baali. Aside from the reasons already mentioned explicitly in the books, another may be that Set is fighting and keeping under control the very entities that Baali threaten to awaken - although some Baali are also trying to keep them asleep, so there's potential for stories about different Setite and Baali factions fighting or working together here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T22:58:28-08:00","id":1545557,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Strangers are the Aeons<br /> Clanbook: Followers of Set Revised defines them clearly; the Aeons are the other Gods than Set and their servants,they take on many other guises but ultimately serve Ra/God; their goal is to enslave humankind, reducing them to a state of senseless obedience with the Laws, the &quot;chains of Ma'at&quot;<br /> While the Strangers goal is to searchvfor flaws in the Nine\u2019s - the Gods - Names, in Creation, so that they might introduce their own words<br /> So they are familiar with the True Name and the related magic<br /> Also the Desert in this case not really phisically the desert souranding Khem<br /> <br /> &quot;Only he ventured beyond the sound of the rushing river, until the sand turned into a substance beyond mortal description.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Set desired to enter the darkness where these Strangers dwelled,&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And he journeyed to the place where the sand became what cannot be said. He walked beyond the world for three nights, or six, or 40. He cast down the Strangers so they would not invade for an age.&quot;<br /> <br /> To me this screams of the Deep Umbra and beyond and the Strangers are Qlippothonic demons<br /> (The Qlippoth (singular Qlippah) are rejected worlds that contain a half-made universe inhabited by creatures from before the creation of the modern Tapestry. - see Mage: Ascension and Infernalism: The Path of Screams)<br /> Also these are VERY similar what is described in the Lilith Cycle and the Revelations of the Dark Mother, remnants and survivors of the previous creations - pointing towards the Baali's Children\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T23:03:36-08:00","id":1545558,"title":"","content":"Theirs always the possibility they dont exist, especially considering set is a manipulative liar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T00:20:15-08:00","id":1545564,"title":"","content":"Ok, I misread the post and got things wrong. Sorry about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T01:03:32-08:00","id":1545565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545419-who-are-the-strangers-from-vda20-companion-s-followers-of-set-apocrypha?p=1545558#post1545558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theirs always the possibility they dont exist, especially considering set is a manipulative liar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but where's the fun in that?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}